.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=FarNitroView

@Contents
$ #FarNitroView#
 FarNitroView shows images right from Far, in the way of the old PictureView plugin, decoded by
the parallel decoders of jpeg-nitro: JPEG (baseline and progressive), PNG, PSD/PSB, HEIC,
DNG, lossy WebP, TIFF, AVIF, SVG and the full-size JPEG inside Canon CR2, Nikon NEF/NRW, Sony ARW and
Fujifilm RAF files. Everything else (GIF, BMP, ICO, JPEG XR, lossless WebP, AVIF/JPEG XL
with the Store extensions ...) goes through Windows Imaging Component.

 PDF files are shown too, through PDFium (pdfium.dll next to the plugin), on #F3#, in the quick
view and from the plugins menu; #Enter# keeps opening them with their own program unless the
option says otherwise. Pages are rendered in the background at the scale they are shown: a slow
one comes in as it is being drawn, and all the keys keep working meanwhile. Password protected
files are not opened; the post-processing (#F6#, #F7#, #F8#) does not apply to PDF pages.

 It is started by
   - #Enter# or #Ctrl-PgDn# on an image (option "Enter archive");
   - #F3# on an image, also inside archives and from Find file (option "View");
   - the quick view panel, #Ctrl-Q# (option "Quick view");
   - the plugins menu (#F11#) in the panels, the viewer and the editor;
   - the command line prefix #nv:# (e.g. nv:photo.jpg).

 Opened on a file of the active panel, the other images of the panel can be paged through
in the panel's order and the selection can be changed. Otherwise the images of the file's
folder are paged through, in name order.

 ~Keys and mouse~@Keys@
 ~Settings~@Config@

@Keys
$ #FarNitroView: keys and mouse#
 #Esc#, #F10#, #Enter#, #Alt-F4#, right click
    Leave. (#F3# too, when opened instead of Far's viewer.)

 #Space#/#BS#, #PgDn#/#PgUp#, #N#/#B#, #2#/#1#, mouse wheel
    Next / previous image. With #Shift# the selection of the current file is inverted first;
    with #Ctrl# the zoom and the position are kept.
    A PDF of several pages: these keys go to its next / previous page (the zoom and the rotation
    stay, the page is shown from its top), and stop at its first and last page. The mouse wheel
    scrolls the page and goes on to the next page at its edge, also stopping at the first and
    last page. In a PDF of one page the wheel goes on to the next file.

 #Alt# with the keys above / #Alt-Shift#
    Next / previous page of a multi-page file / 20 pages at a time.
    In a PDF #Alt# goes to the next / previous file instead.

 #P#
    Paging goes through the pages too, as if each page were a file.

 #Pause#
    Pause / resume an animation.

 #Home#/#End#, #R#/#T#
    First / last image.

 #~~#
    Back to the previously shown image (and again: forth), keeping the position.

 #F#, #Numpad 5#, #Alt-Enter#, middle click
    Full screen on / off.

 #*#, #9#
    Zoom 100%. A PDF page is fitted into the window instead.

 #/#, #0#, #Tab#, double click on the image
    Toggle: fit to the screen / 100%. A PDF page: fit to the screen / to the width.

 #*#, #9#, #/#, #0#, #Tab# with #Ctrl# / #Shift# / #Alt#
    Fit to the screen / to the width / to the height.

 Double click on the background
    Fit to the width or the height, whichever fills the screen.

 #+#/#-#, #E#/#Q#, wheel with the left button (or #Ctrl#) held
    Zoom in / out in √2 steps, stopping at 100% and at the fitted size; with #Alt# in small
    steps, smaller still with #Ctrl-Alt#. The wheel zooms around the mouse pointer.

 Arrows, #W#/#A#/#S#/#D#, dragging with the mouse
    Move a zoomed image; #Alt#: small steps, smaller with #Ctrl-Alt#; #Ctrl#: slow.

 #Ins#/#Del#
    Select / unselect the current file (panel only).

 #Ctrl-Ins#
    Copy the title (file, size, zoom, decoder) to the clipboard.

 #F3#/#F4#, #[#/#]#
    Rotate 90° counter-clockwise / clockwise (#Shift# reverses).

 #F9#/#F11#
    Mirror left-right / upside down.

 #F6#, #F7#, #F8#
    Post-processing: more colour (chroma) / automatic brightness / automatic levels.

 #F12#
    Undo the post-processing, rotations and mirrors (back to the EXIF orientation).

 #F5#
    Reload the image.

 #I#
    Information line on / off.

 #F1#, #F2#
    This help, the ~settings~@Config@.

@Config
$ #FarNitroView: settings#
 #Enter archive#      Open images on Enter and Ctrl-PgDn.
 #Quick view#         Show images in the quick view panel.
 #View#               Open images with FarNitroView instead of Far's viewer (F3).

 #Fullscreen on startup#  Start in full screen instead of over the console window.
 #Smooth scaling#         Bilinear filtering when enlarging (reduction is always
                         area-averaged; integer zoom levels are pixel exact).
 #Show information line#  File name, position, size, zoom and decoder over the image
                         (off by default: the window title shows the same; I toggles it).

 #Autosize on image open# Large images are fitted to the screen; otherwise 100%.
 #Enlarge small images#   Fitting enlarges small images too (PDF pages always).

 #Open PDF files#         Show PDF files on F3 and in the quick view (needs pdfium.dll).
 #Enter opens PDFs here too#  Enter and Ctrl-PgDn too, instead of their own program.
 #Fit to width on open#   PDF pages open as wide as the window, from the top; otherwise as
                         "Autosize on image open" says. 100% is the page at 96 dpi.

 #Keep position on jumps# The zoom and the position stay when going to another image.
 #Loop jumping#           After the last image the first, before the first the last.

 #Background#  Colours (hexadecimal RRGGBB) around the image and behind transparency;
"Selected" is used for selected files.

 #Post-processing#  Which of auto-levels (F8), auto-luma (F7) and chroma (F6) are on when
the viewer opens, and how much chroma multiplies the colour saturation.

 #Title template#  What the window title shows: {name} {path} {dir} {index} {count} {width}
{height} {zoom} {decoder} {ms} {size} {page} {pages} {pageinfo} {pp} {selected}.

 #Command line prefix#  The prefix for the command line (default nv).
